#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-reflog(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:7
msgid "git-reflog - Manage reflog information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git reflog' [show] [<log-options>] [<ref>]\n"
"'git reflog list'\n"
"'git reflog expire' [--expire=<time>] [--expire-unreachable=<time>]\n"
"\t[--rewrite] [--updateref] [--stale-fix]\n"
"\t[--dry-run | -n] [--verbose] [--all [--single-worktree] | <refs>...]\n"
"'git reflog delete' [--rewrite] [--updateref]\n"
"\t[--dry-run | -n] [--verbose] <ref>@{<specifier>}...\n"
"'git reflog exists' <ref>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:24
msgid "This command manages the information recorded in the reflogs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:32
msgid ""
"Reference logs, or \"reflogs\", record when the tips of branches and other "
"references were updated in the local repository. Reflogs are useful in "
"various Git commands, to specify the old value of a reference. For example, "
"`HEAD@{2}` means \"where HEAD used to be two moves ago\", "
"`master@{one.week.ago}` means \"where master used to point to one week ago "
"in this local repository\", and so on. See linkgit:gitrevisions[7] for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:35
msgid ""
"The command takes various subcommands, and different options depending on "
"the subcommand:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:42
msgid ""
"The \"show\" subcommand (which is also the default, in the absence of any "
"subcommands) shows the log of the reference provided in the command-line (or "
"`HEAD`, by default). The reflog covers all recent actions, and in addition "
"the `HEAD` reflog records branch switching.  `git reflog show` is an alias "
"for `git log -g --abbrev-commit --pretty=oneline`; see linkgit:git-log[1] "
"for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:44
msgid "The \"list\" subcommand lists all refs which have a corresponding reflog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:50
msgid ""
"The \"expire\" subcommand prunes older reflog entries. Entries older than "
"`expire` time, or entries older than `expire-unreachable` time and not "
"reachable from the current tip, are removed from the reflog.  This is "
"typically not used directly by end users -- instead, see linkgit:git-gc[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:55
msgid ""
"The \"delete\" subcommand deletes single entries from the reflog. Its "
"argument must be an _exact_ entry (e.g. \"`git reflog delete "
"master@{2}`\"). This subcommand is also typically not used directly by end "
"users."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:59
msgid ""
"The \"exists\" subcommand checks whether a ref has a reflog.  It exits with "
"zero status if the reflog exists, and non-zero status if it does not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `show`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:67
msgid "`git reflog show` accepts any of the options accepted by `git log`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `expire`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:74
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--all::`\n"
"\tProcess the reflogs of all references.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--single-worktree::`\n"
"\tBy default when `--all` is specified, reflogs from all working\n"
"\ttrees are processed. This option limits the processing to reflogs\n"
"\tfrom the current working tree only.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:87
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--expire=<time>::`\n"
"\tPrune entries older than the specified time. If this option is\n"
"\tnot specified, the expiration time is taken from the\n"
"\tconfiguration setting `gc.reflogExpire`, which in turn\n"
"\tdefaults to 90 days. `--expire=all` prunes entries regardless\n"
"\tof their age; `--expire=never` turns off pruning of reachable\n"
"\tentries (but see `--expire-unreachable`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--expire-unreachable=<time>::`\n"
"\tPrune entries older than `<time>` that are not reachable from\n"
"\tthe current tip of the branch. If this option is not\n"
"\tspecified, the expiration time is taken from the configuration\n"
"\tsetting `gc.reflogExpireUnreachable`, which in turn defaults\n"
"\tto 30 days. `--expire-unreachable=all` prunes unreachable\n"
"\tentries regardless of their age; `--expire-unreachable=never`\n"
"\tturns off early pruning of unreachable entries (but see\n"
"\t`--expire`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--updateref::`\n"
"\tUpdate the reference to the value of the top reflog entry (i.e.\n"
"\t<ref>@\\{0\\}) if the previous top entry was pruned.  (This\n"
"\toption is ignored for symbolic references.)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--rewrite::`\n"
"\tIf a reflog entry's predecessor is pruned, adjust its \"old\"\n"
"\tSHA-1 to be equal to the \"new\" SHA-1 field of the entry that\n"
"\tnow precedes it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--stale-fix::`\n"
"\tPrune any reflog entries that point to \"broken commits\". A\n"
"\tbroken commit is a commit that is not reachable from any of\n"
"\tthe reference tips and that refers, directly or indirectly, to\n"
"\ta missing commit, tree, or blob object.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:118
msgid ""
"This computation involves traversing all the reachable objects, i.e. it has "
"the same cost as 'git prune'.  It is primarily intended to fix corruption "
"caused by garbage collecting using older versions of Git, which didn't "
"protect objects referred to by reflogs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-n::`\n"
"`--dry-run::`\n"
"\tDo not actually prune any entries; just show what would have\n"
"\tbeen pruned.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--verbose::`\n"
"\tPrint extra information on screen.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for `delete`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-reflog.txt:134
msgid ""
"`git reflog delete` accepts options `--updateref`, `--rewrite`, `-n`, "
"`--dry-run`, and `--verbose`, with the same meanings as when they are used "
"with `expire`."
msgstr ""

